Subject: [PATCH] accept a character device as a jobserver

The jobserver token protocol only needs read(2)/write(2), so a character
device serving tokens (e.g. a CUSE device such as /dev/steve) is as valid a
transport as a named pipe.

Backport of upstream 71cb2a4d69 ("Permit jobserver on character device in
addition to a named pipe"), which landed after v1.13.2.
---
--- a/src/jobserver-posix.cc
+++ b/src/jobserver-posix.cc
@@ -26,11 +26,12 @@
 
 namespace {
 
-// Return true if |fd| is a fifo or pipe descriptor.
+// Return true if |fd| is a fifo or a character device.
 bool IsFifoDescriptor(int fd) {
   struct stat info;
   int ret = ::fstat(fd, &info);
-  return (ret == 0) && ((info.st_mode & S_IFMT) == S_IFIFO);
+  return (ret == 0) && (((info.st_mode & S_IFMT) == S_IFIFO) ||
+                        ((info.st_mode & S_IFMT) == S_IFCHR));
 }
 
 // Implementation of Jobserver::Client for Posix systems
